Affected: at 092d76c scripts/prune-target.sh deletes ANY file older than the
prune age, including build-script OUT_DIR contents and fingerprints. An
OUT_DIR file can be old while its fingerprint is fresh, so cargo consumes the
half-missing build without re-running the build script. Observed for real
immediately after the first prune: compiling tree-sitter v0.26.11 failed with
"couldn't read target/debug/build/tree-sitter-<hash>/out/stdlib-symbols.txt:
No such file or directory" at binding_rust/lib.rs:3848 (include_str! of
OUT_DIR output whose file the prune had deleted).

Reproduction: scripts/test_prune_target.py seeds a stale OUT_DIR file, a
stale fingerprint, and a stale deps artifact, runs the prune, and requires
the first two to survive and the third to be deleted. At 092d76c it exits 1
(both OUT_DIR file and fingerprint pruned); with the fix (build/ and
.fingerprint/ subtrees excluded from the file-age prune) it exits 0.
Recovery on the affected machine was a full cargo clean.
